.TH TCPPING 1 "May 2026" "tcpping 1.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tcpping \- measure TCP round-trip latency using the TCP three-way handshake
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tcpping
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIHOSTNAME\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tcpping
measures the round-trip time (RTT) latency between the local host and a remote
server by timing the TCP three-way handshake.
It sends a SYN packet, waits for the SYN\-ACK, then immediately closes the
connection and reports the elapsed time.
.PP
By default,
.B tcpping
runs indefinitely until interrupted with
.BR Ctrl\-C ,
at which point it prints a statistics summary.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-4 ", " \-\-ipv4
Use IPv4 (default).
.TP
.BR \-6 ", " \-\-ipv6
Use IPv6.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-audible
Emit a terminal bell character on each ping.
.TP
.BI \-c " COUNT" ", \-\-count " COUNT
Stop after \fICOUNT\fR pings.
Without this option, pinging continues until interrupted.
.TP
.BI \-p " PORT" ", \-\-port " PORT
Connect to \fIPORT\fR (default: 443).
.TP
.BI \-i " SEC" ", \-\-interval " SEC
Wait \fISEC\fR seconds between pings (default: 1).
.TP
.BI \-s " COUNT" ", \-\-skip " COUNT
Exclude the first \fICOUNT\fR pings from statistics (default: 0).
Useful to let the connection warm up before measuring.
.TP
.BI \-t " SEC" ", \-\-timeout " SEC
Wait \fISEC\fR seconds before declaring a ping timed out (default: 3).
.TP
.BI \-d " MODE" ", \-\-display " MODE
Control output verbosity.
.RS
.TP
.B all
Print each ping result and final statistics (default).
.TP
.B stat
Print only the final statistics block.
.TP
.B clean
Print minimal key=value statistics suitable for scripted parsing.
.RE
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display a usage summary and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Display version information and exit.
.SH EXAMPLES
Ping example.com on the default port (443) until interrupted:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
tcpping example.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Send 5 pings to TCP port 22 (SSH) using IPv4:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
tcpping \-4 \-c 5 \-p 22 example.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Ping using IPv6, showing only the final statistics:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
tcpping \-6 \-c 10 \-d stat example.com
.EE
.RE
.PP
Warm up with 3 skipped pings, then collect 10 measured pings:
.PP
.RS 4
.EX
tcpping \-s 3 \-c 13 example.com
.EE
.RE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Hostname lookup failed.
